## Wrong + high grounding (llm_only, code_rule; A12 cut 0.75): 23 candidates (llm_only 11, code_rule 12)

**1. llm_only re2tt_ts-auth-service_cpu_2**: truth ts-auth-service, final ts-ui-dashboard, H_E001a ts-auth-service, grounding 1.000, 4 expl claims
- [stru/root-cause] P (partly): ts-ui-dashboard is the root-cause service of this incident.
- [stru/root-cause] P (partly): The fault category is delay.
- [stru/root-cause] S (yes): The anomaly indicator is ts-ui-dashboard_latency-90.
- [expl/observational] S (yes): The ts-ui-dashboard_latency-90 metric had a standardized mean shift of +88.0%, x1.88, shift=9.8, indicating a significant increase in latency.
- [expl/observational] S (yes): The ts-auth-service showed a large increase in latency-50 by 235.7%, x3.36.
- [expl/observational] S (yes): The decrease in socket metrics for ts-train-mongo did not show a sharp onset.
- [expl/observational] S (yes): No logs or traces provided evidence of health issues for ts-train-mongo.

**2. code_rule re2ss_orders_delay_1**: truth orders, final shipping, H_E001a shipping, grounding 1.000, 4 expl claims
- [stru/root-cause] P (partly): shipping is the root-cause service of this incident.
- [stru/root-cause] S (yes): The fault category is delay.
- [stru/root-cause] S (yes): The anomaly indicator is shipping_latency-90.
- [expl/observational] S (yes): The shipping service experienced a change of +4266.0% in shipping_latency-90.
- [expl/observational] S (yes): The shipping service had a shift of 853.2 in shipping_latency-90.
- [expl/observational] S (yes): The payment service had a shift of 836.0.
- [expl/causal] S (yes): The shipping service's shift in shipping_latency-90 was larger than the payment service's shift.

**3. llm_only re2tt_ts-route-service_delay_2**: truth ts-route-service, final ts-payment-service, H_E001a ts-route-service, grounding 1.000, 3 expl claims
- [stru/root-cause] U (absent): ts-payment-service is the root-cause service of this incident.
- [stru/root-cause] U (yes): The fault category is cpu.
- [stru/root-cause] S (yes): The anomaly indicator is ts-payment-service_cpu.
- [expl/observational] S (yes): The metric 'ts-payment-service_cpu' shows a significant increase of 82.9%, from 0.20 to 0.36 mean CPU usage, after the onset of the incident.
- [expl/observational] S (yes): The metric 'ts-order-service' latency metrics also showed an increase.
- [expl/causal] S (yes): The CPU metric for 'ts-payment-service' more directly indicates a resource constraint leading to performance degradation.

**4. code_rule re2tt_ts-order-service_disk_3**: truth ts-order-service, final ts-train-service, H_E001a ts-order-service, grounding 1.000, 3 expl claims
- [stru/root-cause] U (partly): ts-train-service is the root-cause service of this incident.
- [stru/root-cause] P (partly): The fault category is cpu.
- [stru/root-cause] S (yes): The anomaly indicator is ts-travel-service_cpu.
- [expl/observational] S (yes): The CPU usage of ts-train-service increased significantly to 0.6141 from 0.361 after the incident onset.
- [expl/observational] S (yes): ts-travel-service's CPU usage increased to 1.10 from 0.78.
- [expl/observational] S (yes): Calls in ts-train-service took up to 67,809 milliseconds.

**5. llm_only re2ss_orders_disk_1**: truth orders, final rabbitmq-exporter, H_E001a catalogue-db, grounding 0.900, 5 expl claims
